5252	{"artifactId":"SPEC-85236f6960022cbc","entry":{"id":"migrated-SPEC-85236f6960022cbc-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-09-23T17:25:40.179Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"brainstorm","stage":"brainstorm","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"cl1","ref":"decision-3/intent","kind":"external-contract","severity":"MED","premise":"A daemon-owned IPC method for updating the daemon (e.g. 'maintenance.update') that pulls+rebuilds+respawns exists or is the intended surface; today the daemon handler map has no such maintenance.* update IPC (the plugins shell out to daemon-ctl.sh update instead), so this is a net-new daemon capability to build.","evidence":"Direct source check: the daemon handler map registers only 'daemon.backup', 'daemon.compact', 'daemon.debug-status', 'daemon.shutdown', 'daemon.status' — there is NO 'maintenance.*' IPC and no 'daemon.update'/'daemon.restart'/'daemon.respawn'. The update runs as an external script (scripts/daemon-ctl.sh update, git fetch + merge --ff-only), which both plugins currently SHELL OUT to (JetBrains 'UPDATE -> daemon-ctl.sh update'; VS Code LifecycleAction 'update' via the controller). So the SPEC/decision-3 wording 'runs the EXISTING update/restart service functions in-process' overstates today's reality: the daemon-owned update IPC does NOT exist — it is NET-NEW, and it must wrap the daemon-ctl.sh logic.","action":"Non-blocking for a requirements SPEC, but the design stage MUST size decision-3 as building a NEW daemon IPC (wrapping the existing daemon-ctl.sh update logic), not calling an existing one. Recommend the DEF/HLD note explicitly: 'maintenance.update' is a new daemon capability; the plugins move from shelling out to daemon-ctl.sh to calling this IPC.","fixability":"assisted"},{"claimId":"cl2","ref":"intent/decision-3","kind":"external-contract","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon does NOT self-restart/respawn via IPC today (restart-after-update is the load-bearing gap the feature must add) — there is no daemon IPC that respawns the daemon process.","evidence":"Confirmed: no daemon self-restart/respawn IPC exists — the only lifecycle-ish IPC is 'daemon.shutdown'; restart/respawn is done externally by daemon-ctl.sh (kill + re-spawn the process). The SPEC CORRECTLY identifies restart-after-update as the load-bearing gap to build (a daemon respawning itself mid-request over IPC is genuinely net-new and is the crux the user flagged). Verified sound — the spec's framing matches reality.","action":"None — the SPEC accurately flags the self-restart gap. The design must solve daemon self-respawn (e.g. the daemon spawns a detached updater that rebuilds + restarts it, then the plugin reconnects).","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl3","ref":"decision-1/citation-c2","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon ships updates via scripts/daemon-ctl.sh update (git pull + rebuild), the unversioned rolling-release mechanism the git-commit-comparison detection is built on.","evidence":"Confirmed: scripts/daemon-ctl.sh update does `git -C $DAEMON_ROOT fetch origin <branch>` + `merge --ff-only` + rev-parse HEAD vs origin/branch (lines 81-104) — the unversioned rolling-release mechanism the git-commit-comparison detection (decision-1) is correctly built on. The rev-parse HEAD vs origin/branch is exactly the commit comparison the plugin will mirror via a remote check.","action":"None — verified sound; daemon-ctl.sh already computes current-vs-incoming commit, a useful reference for the detection design.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl4","ref":"intent/decision-1","kind":"external-contract","severity":"LOW","premise":"A daemon.status IPC exists today (the feature adds a lightweight installed-git-commit field to it, or a sibling IPC), so the plugin can read the daemon's installed commit over the existing socket.","evidence":"Confirmed: the 'daemon.status' IPC handler exists at src/daemon/index.ts:922. So decision-1's 'lightweight daemon.status field/IPC' reporting the installed git commit is feasible as an additive field on the existing status handler.","action":"None — verified sound.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl5","ref":"intent","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"Both plugins already have a daemon update action wired to daemon-ctl.sh update today (VS Code LifecycleAction 'update'; JetBrains DaemonLifecycle UPDATE -> daemon-ctl.sh update), which this feature re-points at the new daemon IPC (or augments with the startup check + self-update trigger).","evidence":"Confirmed: VS Code has LifecycleAction 'update' (controller.ts:16) and JetBrains maps UPDATE -> daemon-ctl.sh update (DaemonLifecycleContracts.kt:45) — both plugins already have a daemon-update action shelling out to the script, which this feature augments (startup check + self-update trigger) and re-points at the new daemon IPC.","action":"None — verified sound; the existing update actions are the natural integration point.","fixability":"auto"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":4},"reviewedAt":"2026-09-23T17:25:40.179Z","model":"client"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
